# Requisições de teste para a extensão "REST Client" (humao.rest-client) do VS Code.
# Clique em "Send Request" acima de cada bloco, na ordem (os blocos usam o resultado dos anteriores).
# Se os e-mails já existirem de uma execução anterior, o cadastro dá 409: troque os e-mails.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Criar a Ana (a carteira é criada junto)
# @name createUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Souza",
  "email": "ana@email.com",
  "password": "senha1234"
}

### 2. Login da Ana: devolve o token JWT
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@email.com",
  "password": "senha1234"
}

### 3. Criar o Bruno
# @name createUser2
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bruno Lima",
  "email": "bruno@email.com",
  "password": "senha1234"
}

### 4. Login do Bruno
# @name login2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bruno@email.com",
  "password": "senha1234"
}

### 5. Minha carteira (Ana): saldo 0.00
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Ana deposita 100,50
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-001

{ "amount": 100.50 }

### 7. Mesmo depósito reenviado (mesma Idempotency-Key): devolve a operação original, saldo não muda
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-001

{ "amount": 100.50 }

### 8. Ana saca 30
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 30 }

### 9. Saque maior que o saldo: 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 9999 }

### 10. Valor inválido (3 casas decimais): 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 10.555 }

### 11. Idempotency-Key reutilizada com outro valor: 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-001

{ "amount": 5 }

### 12. Ana transfere 20 para o Bruno
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tr-001

{
  "targetWalletId": "{{createUser2.response.body.walletId}}",
  "amount": 20
}

### 13. Carteira do Bruno (com o token dele): saldo 20.00
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login2.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14. Transferência maior que o saldo: 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetWalletId": "{{createUser2.response.body.walletId}}",
  "amount": 99999
}

### 15. Transferir para a própria carteira: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetWalletId": "{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}",
  "amount": 10
}

### 16. Carteira de destino inexistente: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser.response.body.walletId}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "targetWalletId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "amount": 10
}

### 17. SEM token: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/me

### 18. Ana tentando ver a carteira do Bruno: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser2.response.body.walletId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 19. Ana tentando sacar da carteira do Bruno: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{createUser2.response.body.walletId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1 }

### 20. Login com senha errada: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@email.com",
  "password": "senha-errada"
}

### 21. Pegar o id da carteira da Ana (precisa do login do bloco 2)
# @name myWallet
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 22. Extrato completo, mais recente primeiro
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{myWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 23. Paginado: 2 por página, página 0 (confira totalElements e totalPages)
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{myWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions?page=0&size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 24. Segunda página
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{myWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions?page=1&size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 25. Só depósitos
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{myWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions?type=DEPOSIT
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 26. Por período (datas inclusivas, fuso de São Paulo)
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{myWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 27. Tipo inválido: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{myWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions?type=PIX
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 28. Tamanho de página acima do limite (100): 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/wallets/{{myWallet.response.body.id}}/transactions?size=1000
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
